    "result_text": "The full test suite is exactly these two acceptance tests, and both pass with a clean `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned the identity key and duplicate detection in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java` to match the spec.\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **`identityKey(Owner)`** \u2014 now returns the lower-case hex SHA-256 of `normalizedTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName)` (via the existing `Owner.sha256HexLower`), replacing the old plain `telephone|email|householdId` concatenation. Email and telephone are already normalized upstream; the last name is reduced to its Soundex code.\n\n2. **New `soundex(String)` + `soundexDigit(char)` helpers** \u2014 a standard American Soundex implementation (commons-codec is not on the dependency tree, so no library reliance). Non-letters ignored, H/W-separated same-code letters coded once, vowels act as separators, right-padded to length 4.\n\n3. **`isDuplicate`** \u2014 unchanged logic (exact identity-key match, ignoring soft-deleted owners \u2192 409); the email-domain blocklist still runs first in `normalizeAndValidateFields` (400). This single identity key now subsumes the former household-duplicate check, so no separate `householdId`-based 409 exists.\n\n4. **Soft match (`findPossibleDuplicateOf`)** \u2014 now triggers when `soundex(lastName)` **and** postcode match but the `identityKey` differs (instead of the old \"same normalized last name + different telephone\"). Because telephone is part of the key, two owners with the same last name and postcode but different telephones now differ in key and are created as a soft match rather than rejected with 409.\n\n5. **Doc consistency** \u2014 updated the javadocs and the `openapi.yml` descriptions for `identityKey`, `possibleDuplicate`, and `possibleDuplicateOf`.\n\nThe `identity_key` column (VARCHAR(512)) comfortably holds the 64-char hex. `householdId` is retained for household member counts and membership caps, but no longer feeds the identity key. Both tests (`coreIdentityKeyIsSha256Hex` asserting the 64-hex shape, and `coreRejectsDuplicateIdentity` asserting the collision 409) pass.",
